Kount A1 — the collection dialog's External ID is shown and editable in the admin console.

At this web vault the field is read-only and shown only for a collection that already has an External ID, so an
admin could not type the id Kount Protect gives an account (plan DA, A1; docs/spike-2026-11.md E14). The admin
console's dialog openers (add and edit) pass `isAdminConsoleActive: true`; outside the admin console the field stays
hidden. It follows the name field's editable state, is capped at 300 characters (Bitwarden's limit) and is trimmed on
save, an empty value sent as none; the copy button shows once there is a value. The server already stores
`externalId` on create and on update. Re-cut on web v2026.10.1 from the `kountlabs/vw_web_builds` branch
`collection-external-id` (the dialog was rewritten upstream).

